  "interpretation": "The submitted jobs point to the intended repaired source and recovery run directories, escalation is afterok-gated, and the listed local/remote critical files match byte-for-byte. The active stream runner passes production-provenance arguments, so the running summer now resolves the compatible d6e83132 validator and the pending winter/overlap jobs explicitly select a read-only checksum-named snapshot of the same file. This closes a pre-publication interface mismatch without changing scientific thresholds. The runner now also checks every validator CLI option before launching HICAR, so a future stale validator fails before expensive computation. Required summer/reference publications exist, and no stale downstream publication can be mistaken for a new result. The pending paired-event assessor additionally requires each model provenance block to be PASS and to match the repaired commit frozen in the scientific plan. It accepts exactly one named summer and one named winter event, requires their model and station timestamps to equal the frozen inclusive three-hour axes, and requires the restart, physical, REA-L, SwissMetNet, and OGD reports to identify that event's exact model chunk. Dedicated afterok-gated auditors independently validate and hash each event's 24-, 48-, and 72-hour restart boundaries; the paired verdict depends on both auditors and requires exactly those three passing checkpoints. The early restart-trajectory job reuses 25 immutable forcing records without FDB or fieldextra work, independently restarts at summer hour 48, and must match all eight three-hourly qualification records through hour 72 before the paired verdict can promote. This is an early event-scale gate, not a substitute for the month-long multi-day overlap. Each 72-hour OGD report must expose the exact two 06--06 UTC RhiresD windows, three TabsD days, and 24 post-initial SIS times derived from that event's frozen axis; duplicate, shifted, sparse, or status-only inventories cannot promote. Gridded TabsD temperature and RhiresD precipitation must also remain within the frozen event-level catastrophic-degradation margins relative to REA-L."
